01:31.560 --> 01:36.940
It's Japan vs. Germany. Japan is down by one in the second half. 

01:37.750 --> 01:40.440
The real game starts now.

01:40.440 --> 01:47.460
I believe that Tsubasa's generation could be the one that gives life to Japanese soccer.

01:47.460 --> 01:52.150
Winning this world tournament could be the start of new golden age for Japanese soccer,

01:52.150 --> 01:55.160
where we can aim for the International Cup.

01:58.550 --> 02:01.170
Germany will win this game.

02:01.170 --> 02:05.970
Don't be so sure. You can't beat the Japanese team that easily.

02:07.070 --> 02:09.720
Is that because Tsubasa's a member?

02:09.720 --> 02:10.820
Yeah.

02:11.250 --> 02:18.820
Even our Diaz probably couldn't do 
anything against Schneider or Müller.

02:18.820 --> 02:23.020
Because of their meager experience with winning international games,

02:23.020 --> 02:29.200
this Japanese team, even with Tsubasa, is not one that can take on Germany.

02:29.200 --> 02:33.820
But the experience they gained in this tournament will be precious to them.

02:33.820 --> 02:38.580
The outcome of the tournament is less important than their experience.

02:39.330 --> 02:40.940
You are...?

02:40.940 --> 02:43.630
Sorry to interrupt you.

02:43.630 --> 02:47.850
I'm Katagiri, from the Japanese Soccer Federation.

02:47.850 --> 02:52.350
This would be our first meeting, but I believe you are Coach Barbas, from Argentina,

02:52.350 --> 02:54.880
and Roberto Hongo-san, from Brancos.

02:56.010 --> 03:00.380
After all this time, what do you think of Tsubasa's play?

03:00.380 --> 03:03.900
He's become a talented player, just like I thought he would.

03:05.280 --> 03:11.420
Who'd think a great player like Tsubasa Ohzora would come from Japan?

03:12.910 --> 03:14.460
Roberto Hongo.

03:15.360 --> 03:18.940
Tsubasa is what he is today because of him.

03:19.620 --> 03:24.090
Roberto-san, I'm leaving to rejoin the players.

03:24.090 --> 03:26.940
Do you have some kind of message for Tsubasa?

03:29.010 --> 03:32.460
"Remember page 52 in the notebook."

03:32.950 --> 03:34.780
Please tell him that.

03:34.780 --> 03:36.890
Is that everything?

03:36.890 --> 03:39.060
Yes. He will understand.

03:39.060 --> 03:40.360
Please pardon me.

03:44.460 --> 03:49.770
Tsubasa, there's one thing a soccer player can never forget.

03:49.770 --> 03:54.010
The outcome of this game will depend on whether or not you understand that.

03:57.340 --> 04:02.460
<b>A Message From Roberto</b>

03:57.340 --> 04:02.460
<b>A Message From Roberto</b>

04:04.140 --> 04:06.460
All right! It's only one goal!

04:06.460 --> 04:09.020
Let's turn the tables around in the second half!

04:09.020 --> 04:10.440
Yeah!

04:12.570 --> 04:14.620
He got you, Wakabayashi.

04:14.620 --> 04:15.700
He did!

04:15.700 --> 04:18.240
But he won't again.

04:18.240 --> 04:21.590
I won't make a fool of myself after having taken your place.

04:21.590 --> 04:23.840
Yeah, I'll be counting on that.

04:24.420 --> 04:27.570
Let's use the same formation in the second half.

04:27.570 --> 04:31.710
Be careful of Kartz, because he's about to attack for real.

04:31.710 --> 04:32.940
All right!

04:32.940 --> 04:37.260
Let's try a combination play, so we can somehow score a goal.

04:37.260 --> 04:39.900
Yes, let's do our best, Tsubasa-kun!

04:40.460 --> 04:41.240
Yes!

04:42.670 --> 04:43.800
Takeshi.

04:43.800 --> 04:44.700
Yes.

04:45.430 --> 04:46.700
Listen, Takeshi.

04:50.700 --> 04:56.700
During these international games, our Japanese team has become more cohesive.

04:56.700 --> 04:59.100
We have to make that into a strength to win.

05:00.570 --> 05:04.750
We let Müller have his fun during the first half.

05:04.750 --> 05:06.340
Now let's get 'em in the second half!

05:06.340 --> 05:06.900
Yes!

05:06.900 --> 05:08.520
The opponent is Japan.

05:08.520 --> 05:09.610
Easy as pie.

05:09.610 --> 05:12.070
Japan will give their all during the second half.

05:12.660 --> 05:14.330
Schneider.

05:14.330 --> 05:17.810
The Japanese team has been evolving during this tournament.

05:17.810 --> 05:20.660
It would be best not to underestimate them.

05:20.660 --> 05:26.310
We are responsible for maintaining the German soccer tradition.

05:26.310 --> 05:30.700
Its history can't be tainted, and that's a heavy burden.

05:31.310 --> 05:35.900
We have to show them the best of German soccer until the end!

05:35.900 --> 05:36.700
Yes!

05:37.240 --> 05:41.590
We'll know the number one team of this International Junior Youth Championship at the end of the next thirty minutes.

05:41.590 --> 05:44.910
Neither of the teams have made any player substitutions.

05:44.910 --> 05:46.700
First, we have to tie the game!

05:46.700 --> 05:50.090
Will Japan be able to catch up, despite being a goal behind?

05:50.090 --> 05:52.290
We're counting on you, Japan!

05:52.290 --> 05:54.460
Good luck, Tsubasa-kun!

05:54.460 --> 05:55.220
All right!

05:59.800 --> 06:02.320
The Japanese players are coming onto the pitch again.

06:04.940 --> 06:06.300
Tsubasa.

06:08.190 --> 06:09.340
Katagiri-san!

06:09.340 --> 06:14.260
Tsubasa, remember page 52 of the notebook!

06:14.260 --> 06:16.570
Eh, notebook?

06:17.290 --> 06:19.150
Hey, Tsubasa!

06:19.150 --> 06:20.620
Ah, yeah.

06:21.130 --> 06:22.530
Notebook?

06:22.530 --> 06:25.430
Was he talking about the notebook from Roberto?

06:27.660 --> 06:29.690
The second half starts, and the game resumes.

06:29.690 --> 06:32.140
Ohzora receives the ball and runs forward.

06:33.270 --> 06:34.780
The notebook from Roberto?

06:35.660 --> 06:41.620
In the future, the most strategic position will be midfielder.

06:44.360 --> 06:48.740
He needs to focus on being the goal-scoring playmaker who sets the pace of the game.

06:48.740 --> 06:49.500
Tsubasa-kun!

06:49.950 --> 06:52.500
He takes control of the game.

06:53.420 --> 06:58.220
It told me how important a midfielder is, so I could begin training to be one.

07:01.970 --> 07:04.060
Ohzora advances while dribbling like he always does.

07:05.120 --> 07:08.750
And it also told me how to dribble "South American" style!

07:09.580 --> 07:10.980
Damn it! Stop him!

07:10.980 --> 07:12.100
Come on! Stop him!

07:14.250 --> 07:17.780
He dribbles and sends off a pass!

07:17.780 --> 07:19.340
I won't let you!

07:19.340 --> 07:23.700
What's this?! Kartz tackles and steals the ball! That must have hurt!

07:26.340 --> 07:27.140
Mark him!

07:27.140 --> 07:28.800
Hurry up and mark him!

07:28.800 --> 07:32.080
Page 22 described the specifics of South American soccer,

07:32.080 --> 07:34.350
as well as the preparedness a pro player should have.

07:34.350 --> 07:36.080
And page 52...

07:37.260 --> 07:40.200
Kartz passes the ball over to Schneider successfully.

07:41.260 --> 07:43.980
And Schneider attacks while dribbling! Japan is in danger!

07:43.980 --> 07:46.100
I won't let you through!

07:48.820 --> 07:49.940
Damn it!

07:51.660 --> 07:53.060
He has to be stopped!

07:53.060 --> 07:54.660
He won't score a second time!

07:54.660 --> 07:55.300
Yeah!

07:57.310 --> 08:00.820
Will the Japanese defense be able to stop Schneider?

08:00.820 --> 08:03.660
Oh! Schneider makes a surprising pass!

08:02.340 --> 08:03.660
This one's mine!

08:04.100 --> 08:05.980
Schester gets the ball and shoots!

08:07.150 --> 08:09.340
Wakabayashi returns the ball without being able to catch it.

08:09.340 --> 08:11.340
Go for the counter!

08:11.340 --> 08:14.620
Hyuga and Sawada follow the returned ball.

08:14.620 --> 08:15.830
Let's do it, Takeshi!

08:15.830 --> 08:16.700
Yes!

08:23.880 --> 08:26.660
This shot won't fool me!

08:27.860 --> 08:29.480
W-What?!

08:29.480 --> 08:33.570
It's our Drive Ball that uses the difference in strength between Huga-san's kicking and mine!

08:33.570 --> 08:36.220
It's not a shot, but a pass to Misaki!

08:36.940 --> 08:37.940
No way!

08:45.280 --> 08:46.820
He's blocking it...

08:46.820 --> 08:49.010
Keep it up, Misaki-kun!

08:49.580 --> 08:50.460
I'm coming, too!

08:50.460 --> 08:51.340
What?!

08:52.700 --> 08:53.900
Here we go!

08:57.660 --> 09:00.140
It's in! Goal!

09:00.980 --> 09:05.100
The Ohzora-Misaki duo broke through the Müller bastion!

09:05.100 --> 09:06.010
Tsubasa!

09:06.010 --> 09:06.620
Misaki-san!

09:06.620 --> 09:08.880
All right, we're tied!

09:08.880 --> 09:15.540
Japan did it! Ten minutes into this second half, Japan scored against Germany's "invincible" Deuter Müller,

09:15.540 --> 09:18.130
making it a 1-1 tie game!

09:18.130 --> 09:20.910
Splendid, Japanese Golden Duo!

09:24.600 --> 09:26.100
Incredible, Japan!

09:26.100 --> 09:29.260
Way to go, Tsubasa-kun! Come on!

09:33.510 --> 09:36.440
They scored a goal against Müller, eh?

09:36.440 --> 09:39.030
Well, all they did was put us back to square one.

09:39.030 --> 09:39.980
Kartz!

09:40.530 --> 09:42.820
This is not a practice game!

09:44.230 --> 09:46.300
Don't get so angry.

09:49.820 --> 09:52.360
Let's score one more goal, Tsubasa.

09:52.360 --> 09:53.230
Yes!

09:53.880 --> 09:57.390
Katagiri-san talked about page 52 of the notebook.

09:57.390 --> 10:02.470
I see! Roberto came here!

10:02.470 --> 10:06.620
Roberto has surely been watching me from the stands.

10:11.260 --> 10:12.810
Roberto...

10:15.950 --> 10:21.330
Roberto, watch the way I play soccer!

10:22.350 --> 10:25.320
He noticed you're here.

10:26.090 --> 10:27.580
He sure did.

10:27.580 --> 10:33.700
What was that advice you had sent to Tsubasa?

10:33.700 --> 10:39.140
Oh, it was just something every soccer player knows.

10:39.140 --> 10:41.700
Something every player knows?

10:41.700 --> 10:42.980
Yeah.

10:43.610 --> 10:50.140
But I felt Tsubasa had it in him ever since I first met him.

10:53.500 --> 10:55.470
The game resumes.

10:55.470 --> 11:00.180
After the equalizer, Herman Kartz dribbles the ball forward.

11:03.670 --> 11:06.980
At the peak of Grünwald's and the Junior Youth teams,

11:10.890 --> 11:13.480
with me defending the goal and Schneider attacking,

11:13.480 --> 11:17.700
it was Kartz who made it possible to win during the tight games.

11:20.700 --> 11:25.420
What kind of play will Kartz show now that he's serious?

11:25.420 --> 11:28.580
That's something not even I, or Schneider, can predict!

11:29.220 --> 11:30.460
Take this!

11:30.460 --> 11:31.780
Here I go!

11:31.780 --> 11:35.220
The two players collide, and they're evenly matched!

11:35.220 --> 11:37.220
Not bad!

11:39.180 --> 11:42.610
The lost ball goes to Schneider.

11:42.610 --> 11:45.540
Oh, is Schneider going for a shot on goal?

11:45.540 --> 11:46.500
Here it comes!

11:51.220 --> 11:52.060
There!

11:54.140 --> 11:55.790
He deflected it!

11:55.790 --> 11:58.180
The ball bounces off the crossbar and clears over the goal.

11:58.180 --> 12:00.460
Wakabayashi deflected the shot!

12:00.460 --> 12:02.540
Way to go, Wakabayashi-kun!

12:05.320 --> 12:07.530
That's really something, Wakabayashi.

12:07.530 --> 12:12.140
We were always equals before, but that was during practice.

12:12.980 --> 12:19.030
But will you be able to stop all my Fire Shots during a real game?

12:21.820 --> 12:23.610
Come at me, Schneider!

12:27.820 --> 12:30.660
Oh, is Schneider going for a shot on goal?

12:30.660 --> 12:31.700
Here it comes!

12:36.460 --> 12:37.380
There!

12:39.100 --> 12:40.460
He deflected it!

12:40.460 --> 12:42.890
The ball bounces off the crossbar and clears over the goal.

12:42.890 --> 12:45.270
Wakabayashi deflected the shot!

12:45.270 --> 12:47.180
Way to go, Wakabayashi-kun!

12:53.270 --> 12:56.500
But Japan is still not out of danger.

12:56.500 --> 12:59.960
Germany obtained a corner kick. The kick will be taken by that trickster, Kartz.

13:01.820 --> 13:05.530
Both Schneider and Schester are in front of the goal.

13:05.530 --> 13:09.690
However, Margas could also use his height and try a header.

13:10.340 --> 13:12.330
Will it be a direct shot?

13:12.830 --> 13:14.790
Or will he center the ball in front of the goal?

13:19.380 --> 13:21.300
Oh, it's a direct shot!

13:21.300 --> 13:21.980
No way!

13:22.300 --> 13:23.300
In front!

13:25.140 --> 13:26.300
Schneider appears!

13:29.020 --> 13:30.900
Matsuyama and Jito stop the ball!

13:32.910 --> 13:33.780
Schester has it!

13:34.740 --> 13:35.740
All mine!

13:35.740 --> 13:36.900
I'll stop you!

13:40.340 --> 13:42.990
The keeper, Wakabayashi, firmly grips the ball!

13:42.990 --> 13:45.700
Japan is out of danger!

13:45.700 --> 13:47.420
Nice save!

13:47.420 --> 13:49.620
Well done, Misaki!

13:49.620 --> 13:51.660
Wakabayashi-kun...

13:53.680 --> 13:57.660
It'll be better if I concentrate on defending for the time being.

13:58.180 --> 13:59.740
Let's go for it, guys!

13:59.740 --> 14:04.740
The German attack won't stop with this! They'll be back for more!

14:05.620 --> 14:07.800
They somehow got out of that.

14:07.800 --> 14:08.500
Yes.

14:08.500 --> 14:15.450
Most of the Japanese team members have been playing and growing along with Tsubasa

14:15.450 --> 14:17.980
ever since they were young.

14:17.980 --> 14:21.150
That's why Germany won't beat them easily.

14:23.590 --> 14:29.730
Tsubasa, this game is putting your teamwork to the test.

14:29.730 --> 14:33.260
You will need to use all your power in order to stop the German attacks.

14:33.730 --> 14:36.430
Ah, Japan's Sawada loses the ball,

14:36.430 --> 14:38.660
and Germany goes on the attack!

14:41.140 --> 14:42.740
Here I go!

14:47.660 --> 14:49.940
This is incredible!

14:49.940 --> 14:53.020
Germany puts up a tremendous fight to defend their name!

14:55.820 --> 14:57.540
I won't let you!

14:57.540 --> 14:59.220
You...!

15:01.100 --> 15:05.980
But Wakabayashi stops all of the German offensive attacks perfectly.

15:10.260 --> 15:15.460
Even if Wakabayashi-kun is defending the goal, we're still on the defensive.

15:16.470 --> 15:18.260
What should we do?

15:20.420 --> 15:24.980
I guarantee that I can stop a free shot 
from any player other than Schneider!

15:27.800 --> 15:32.380
As I thought, I'm the only one who can score against Wakabayashi.

15:33.600 --> 15:36.730
Don't get too cocky, Wakabayashi.

15:38.710 --> 15:40.100
Oh, what speed!

15:40.100 --> 15:43.100
Kartz rapidly steals the ball away from Japan!

15:47.500 --> 15:49.810
He gets past Ohzora!

15:50.850 --> 15:55.280
Next, he passes all of Japan's defense and is in front of the goal!

15:55.780 --> 15:57.140
As if I'll let you!

15:58.780 --> 16:01.780
Not all shots have to be fast.

16:03.730 --> 16:06.530
Wow, this is a lob from Kartz!

16:06.530 --> 16:08.740
Wakabayashi is taken by surprise!

16:09.180 --> 16:10.460
Yes, I got it!

16:10.460 --> 16:12.040
Wakabayashi-kun!

16:12.040 --> 16:12.580
Wakabayashi!

16:21.340 --> 16:23.590
H-He stopped it!

16:23.590 --> 16:25.580
Wakabayashi, the godly protector of Japan, has just saved his team!

16:26.110 --> 16:29.420
Damn, he stopped it!

16:29.420 --> 16:31.700
Good work, Wakabayashi!

16:31.700 --> 16:33.420
Wakabayashi-san!

16:36.050 --> 16:38.940
That was quite interesting, Kartz.

16:39.450 --> 16:42.430
I don't care what kind of ball you shoot! Fire away!

16:42.430 --> 16:44.100
Let me have some more fun!

16:47.420 --> 16:49.900
Go for it, Tsubasa!

16:53.070 --> 16:54.610
That's it!

17:00.000 --> 17:03.600
Oh, what's the meaning of this? What's going on?

17:03.600 --> 17:06.560
Ohzora, who has the ball, hasn't taken a step.

17:09.140 --> 17:11.620
Page 52 in the notebook!

17:15.330 --> 17:17.730
Now's our chance to steal the ball from him!

17:18.620 --> 17:20.100
Tsubasa-kun!

17:20.100 --> 17:21.630
Tsubasa!

17:22.370 --> 17:24.580
Page 52 in the notebook!

17:26.070 --> 17:30.500
That's it. So that's what it was, Roberto!

17:38.060 --> 17:40.220
I got it, Roberto!

17:40.220 --> 17:45.740
Page 52 talks about how fun it is to play soccer!

17:47.820 --> 17:49.060
I've got it now!

17:52.980 --> 17:54.470
What?!

17:56.960 --> 17:58.900
He's gotten lighter on his feet!

18:00.300 --> 18:03.380
We have to stop him, or else he might be really dangerous.

18:04.820 --> 18:05.700
Stop him!

18:05.700 --> 18:07.520
Stop that guy!

18:10.900 --> 18:13.890
Is there anything wrong, Sis?

18:13.890 --> 18:16.380
Tsubasa-kun's back...

18:17.320 --> 18:18.630
He grew wings!

18:26.760 --> 18:31.780
Tsubasa, why is soccer so fun?

18:33.110 --> 18:38.210
It's because it is the simplest and most free sport!

18:38.940 --> 18:42.780
No matter the position, every player can try to score.

18:43.940 --> 18:49.140
This freedom makes soccer the most appreciated sport throughout the world.

18:49.140 --> 18:51.770
I, too, love this sport.

18:51.770 --> 18:55.040
Tsubasa, if you want to keep playing soccer,

18:55.040 --> 18:58.100
I want you, more than anyone else, to love the thrill of soccer!

18:59.620 --> 19:01.280
Along with your friends!

19:01.280 --> 19:02.100
Take this!

19:05.380 --> 19:07.660
Here goes Ohzora's Drive Shot!

19:07.660 --> 19:09.320
Like I'll let you!

19:10.180 --> 19:13.380
Oh, what's this? Misaki tries to shoot directly!

19:13.860 --> 19:15.540
Go in!

19:15.540 --> 19:16.980
Damn!

19:18.560 --> 19:20.340
It's been stopped!

19:20.820 --> 19:24.740
But Ohzora runs towards the ball!

19:25.340 --> 19:26.860
I'll score from here!

19:28.480 --> 19:30.590
Schneider's running, too!

19:31.370 --> 19:33.260
I'll stop him!

19:34.100 --> 19:36.280
It's a duel between the captains.

19:38.780 --> 19:41.260
It ends in a draw.

19:42.920 --> 19:44.100
Not yet!

19:44.100 --> 19:45.900
It's mine!

19:45.900 --> 19:47.340
Kartz has arrived.

19:48.270 --> 19:51.850
But the ball is still spinning uncontrollably.

19:52.830 --> 19:53.860
What the...?

19:57.400 --> 19:58.060
Damn it!

19:58.060 --> 20:02.070
Incredible! Kartz's attempted steal became a pass to Ohzora!

20:03.840 --> 20:05.180
All right!

20:07.600 --> 20:10.980
The shock from earlier has numbed my leg!

20:10.980 --> 20:13.250
Ohzora prepares to shoot!

20:14.780 --> 20:16.370
What should I do?

20:16.370 --> 20:19.500
Always let your instinct guide you!

20:21.020 --> 20:22.460
I'll stop him!

20:23.460 --> 20:24.540
What?

20:28.700 --> 20:30.780
Ohzora suddenly passes backwards to Hyuga!

20:30.780 --> 20:32.420
Please, Hyuga-kun!

20:32.420 --> 20:33.300
Yes!

20:33.830 --> 20:36.140
Hyuga prepares to shoot!

20:36.140 --> 20:40.540
I'll bet everything on this one shot!

20:40.540 --> 20:42.060
I won't let you score!

20:42.060 --> 20:44.020
Out of the way!

20:44.020 --> 20:46.450
Here's my Neo Tiger Shot!

20:57.640 --> 20:58.900
Goal!

20:59.850 --> 21:03.550
After overcoming a double barrier from Schneider and Müller,

21:03.550 --> 21:06.760
the Neo Tiger Shot flies straight into the German goal!

21:06.760 --> 21:08.430
2-1!

21:08.430 --> 21:11.020
Japan finally turns the game around!

21:11.020 --> 21:13.140
He did it!

21:14.660 --> 21:16.100
Hyuga-san!

21:17.140 --> 21:18.280
We've taken the lead!

21:18.280 --> 21:19.060
Yes!

21:19.060 --> 21:20.740
All right!

21:21.280 --> 21:26.780
To live such moments is why I became a forward!

21:26.780 --> 21:29.540
Nice shot, Hyuga-kun!

21:30.640 --> 21:32.260
Nice assist!

21:33.340 --> 21:37.780
Tsuabsa, I congratulate you for having become such a great player!

21:37.780 --> 21:41.780
The Japanese team did it, and are now leading by one goal!

21:41.780 --> 21:46.090
In this difficult game against the top-seeded German team,

21:46.090 --> 21:48.780
Japan has taken a big leap towards victory!

21:48.780 --> 21:51.720
This Japanese Junior Youth team is amazing!

21:53.920 --> 21:57.780
I'll make sure to get back this goal!

22:03.220 --> 22:08.820
Preview

22:04.860 --> 22:08.460
It's the final in the International Junior Youth Championship in France.

22:08.460 --> 22:14.020
We managed to get a 2-1 lead against Germany in the second half.

22:14.020 --> 22:16.620
We're striving to become the number one youth team in the world.

22:16.620 --> 22:19.020
Just 15 more minutes left.

22:19.020 --> 22:21.130
We'll win for sure!

22:21.130 --> 22:23.270
The world title is right before our eyes!

22:23.270 --> 22:25.060
Next time, on Captain Tsubasa:

22:24.460 --> 22:33.060
Shine in Glory, Japanese Team!

22:25.060 --> 22:26.730
Shine in Glory, Japanese Team!

22:26.730 --> 22:27.980
Look forward to it!

22:27.980 --> 22:30.260
Let's aim for tomorrow. Get goal!

